The negate path overflowed for the minimum of the target type: the magnitude is `max() + 1` (i.e. `2^127` for `HUGEINT`), and negating it is UB (UBSan: signed integer overflow at bignum.hpp:121). The minimum is now assigned from `NumericLimits<T>::Minimum()` when the magnitude equals `max() + 1`:

```cpp
auto max_abs_value = static_cast<uhugeint_t>(NumericLimits<T>::Maximum()) + 1;
if (abs_value > max_abs_value) {
	return false;
}
if (abs_value == max_abs_value) {
	result = NumericLimits<T>::Minimum();
} else {
	result = static_cast<T>(-static_cast<hugeint_t>(abs_value));
}
```

