@Mytherin, regarding 1, this only happens when spill is on (and it is off by default). I think that we should not cater to a setting that is off by default. In fact, what we could do is adapt the minimum block size if the setting is on. But in my opinion that could be a separate PR and is less relevant.

I did address the second point: added some block absorption logic, which threshold is 1/8 of the block size (by default 256KB). This solves the problem for some cases (where the gap is relatively small between columns, again 256KB will not cover a very large gap). As a side effect, most block sizes will be 256 so it will help with problem 1.

Something like TPCH q06 followed by a wide query will still perform a bunch of GETs more for the wide query. However, with the current implementation, q06 cold will be considerably slower and fetch 3x more data, so you win some you loose some. This branch wins more than looses in my opinion.

