Hi @NiclasHaderer, we try our best to limit symbol leakage. This has a few advantages. like reducing the chance of accidental symbol collisions, and reduces binary size, to name a few. We do not want to expose these RE2 symbols.

This is not a problem when using DuckDB with `jemalloc`, as these allocations won't go through `jemalloc`. This is specifically an issue when you're preloading `jemalloc`. I don't think the proper solution is to expose the symbols. Instead, we could patch up RE2. I would be happy to review a PR that does this.

