Thanks for the PR! I think we should simplify this before merging.

TopN and the row-group pruner should only follow cast paths that preserve the raw column's ordering. Replaying arbitrary cast chains means reproducing `TRY_CAST` NULLs and default-cast errors, while `RowGroupPruner` currently ignores the recorded chain. This still produces wrong results:

```sql
SET threads=1;
CREATE TABLE t(k INTEGER);
INSERT INTO t SELECT 0 FROM range(122880);
INSERT INTO t SELECT 1000 FROM range(122880);

SELECT TRY_CAST(k AS TINYINT) AS x
FROM t
ORDER BY x NULLS FIRST
LIMIT 3;
```

This returns three zeroes instead of three NULLs. The issue predates this patch, but it shows that arbitrary cast chains are not a safe shared contract for order-based optimizations.

Could we keep the existing cast-chain reconstruction for join filters, but have TopN and `RowGroupPruner` bail on explicit `TRY_CAST` and any cast that can throw? For the remaining widening integral casts, TopN can cast the raw input directly to the final sort type, and the row-group pruner can safely use the raw statistics.

Thanks for the PR! One comment:

Could we avoid storing the intra-MetaPipeline dependencies twice? The scheduler reads `MetaPipeline::pipeline_dependencies`, while `GetAllDependencies()` reads the mirrored `Pipeline::intra_dependencies`. These are in sync now, but paths such as `CreateUnionPipeline` have to update both manually, so it is easy for them to diverge again.

I think the simplest shape is to make `Pipeline::intra_dependencies` the single source of truth. `MetaPipeline` would only add to it:

```cpp
void Pipeline::AddIntraDependency(Pipeline &dependency) {
	intra_dependencies.emplace_back(dependency.shared_from_this());
}

void MetaPipeline::AddPipelineDependency(Pipeline &dependant, Pipeline &dependency) {
	dependant.AddIntraDependency(dependency);
}
```

`Executor::ScheduleEventsInternal` can then consume the same vector instead of going through `MetaPipeline::GetDependencies()`:

```cpp
for (auto &entry : event_map) {
	auto &pipeline = entry.first.get();
	for (auto &weak_dependency : pipeline.intra_dependencies) {
		auto dependency = weak_dependency.lock();
		D_ASSERT(dependency);
		auto dependency_entry = event_map.find(*dependency);
		D_ASSERT(dependency_entry != event_map.end());
		entry.second.pipeline_event.AddDependency(dependency_entry->second.pipeline_event);
	}
}
```

This lets us remove `MetaPipeline::pipeline_dependencies`. The edges can remain `weak_ptr<Pipeline>` because the executor already keeps all pipelines alive for the query; we do not need a shared dependency container. For unions, maybe add a small `InheritDependencies` helper that copies both the intra- and cross-MetaPipeline dependency vectors.

