The branch is predicated on the active slice:

```cpp
// Limit the validity bitmask slice to the bits left in the current validity word
// and the rows left in the append.
const auto bits_in_entry = MinValue<idx_t>(ValidityMask::BITS_PER_VALUE - idx_in_entry, count - local_offset);
const auto active_mask = ValidityMask::EntryWithValidBits(bits_in_entry);

// Shift the current validity bitmask slice down to bit 0 and mask off rows outside the slice.
const auto valid_bits = (entry >> idx_in_entry) & active_mask;
```

So if `bits_in_entry` is 5:

```
active_mask = 0b11111
// some entry could be loaded, lets say its 0b01010111
entry = validity.GetValidityEntryUnsafe(entry_idx)

// validity mask looks like
bit:       7 6 5 4 3 2 1 0
entry:     0 1 0 1 0 1 1 1
active:          ^ ^ ^ ^ ^
                 4 3 2 1 0

// the shift looks like thi:
valid_bits = entry & active_mask
            = 0b01010111
            & 0b00011111
            = 0b00010111

// and the branches
valid_bits != active_mask   // 0b10111 != 0b11111
valid_bits != 0             // 0b10111 != 0b00000

// so we fall through
```

